{"id":"word:hebrew:H996","type":"word","title":"בֵּין","subtitle":"H996 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"between (repeated before each noun, often with other particles); also as a conjunction, either ... or","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to בֵּין (H996) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: prep.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 410 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"בֵּין (bêyn) means between (repeated before each noun, often with other particles); also as a conjunction, either ... or First listed occurrence: 1Chr 21 16."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"בֵּין","transliteration":"bêyn","pronunciation":"bane","strong":"H996","lemmaId":"hebrew:H996","partOfSpeech":"prep","forms":["בֵּ֥ין","וּ/בֵ֥ין","וּ/בֵ֣ין","בֵּ֣ין","בֵּֽין"],"morphs":[["HR",172],["HC/R",120],["HR/Sp1cs",31],["HR/R",19],["HC/R/Sp2ms",17],["HR/Sp1cp",11],["HC/R/Sp2mp",10],["HR/Sp3mp",8],["HR/Sp3ms",5],["HC/R/R",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"between (repeated before each noun, often with other particles); also as a conjunction, either ... or","usage":"among, asunder, at, between (-twixt...and), + from (the widest), × in, out of, whether (it be...or), within.","full":"H996. bayin [ בַּ֫יִן ] substantive properly interval, space between ( id. ) — construct בֵּין once Isa 44:4 (Baer) בֵּינוֺ בֵינֵךְ, ֵבּינְךָ, בֵּינִי, בֵּן, ( בֵּינָיו Josh 3:4 ; 8:11 Qr); with plural suffix in plural form בֵּינֵינוּ ( בֵּנֵינוּ ), etc.; also בֵּינוֺת Ezek 10:2 (twice in verse); 10:6 (twice in verse); 10:7 (twice in verse) (+ 1:13 ᵐ5 Hi Ew etc. for דְּמוּת ), בֵּינוֺתֵינוּ Gen 26:28 ; Josh 22:34 ; Judg 11:10 , בֵּינוֺתָם Gen 42:23 ; 2Sam 21:7 ; Jer 25:16 ; dual בֵּנַיִם (see below); — 1 always (except dual) as preposition in the interval of , between (so Aramaic בֵּין , & plural בֵּינֵי , , ; ), as Gen 15:17 הַגְּזָרִים בֵּין between the pieces, Exod 13:9 and elsewhere עֵינֶיךָ בֵּין between thy eyes (see עַיִן ), Isa 22:11 and elsewhere between the two walls (see חוֺמָה ), Job 24:11 ; 30:7 ; Job 40:30 part him between merchants; rather more Generally among Hosea 13:15 ; Song 2:2-3 , Ezek 19:2 ; 31:3 ; Job 34:37 ; less exactly within Prov 26:13 a lion is הָֽרְחֹבוֺת בֵּין within the board places (compare 23:13 בְּתוֺךְ ): once with a singular (unusual) Dan 8:16 אוּלַי בֵּין between the Ulai, i.e. between its banks. When the space separating two distinct objects is to be indicated, this is done a. most commonly by repeating בין , as Gen 13:3 הָעָ֑י וּבֵין בֵּיתְאֵל בֵּין literally in the interval of Bethel, and in the interval of `Ai, i.e. between Bethel and `Ai, 16:14 ; 17:7 ; 31:50-51 , +? b. more rarely by לְ ֗֗֗ בֵּין , Gen 1:6 dividing לָמָ֑יִם מַיִם בֵּין literally in the interval of waters with reference to waters, i.e. between the waters and the waters, Lev 20:25 ; 27:33 ; Deut 17:8 (3 t. in verse); 2Sam 19:36 ; 1Kin 3:9 ; Ezek 41:18 ; 42:20 ; 44:23 (twice in verse); Jonah 4:11 ; Mal 3:18 (twice in verse); 2Chr 14:10 . c. by וּלְ ֗֗֗ בֵּין Joel 2:17 . d. by לְבֵין ֗֗֗ בֵּין Isa 59:2 . בֵּין is used not only of actual locality, but also with verbs of dividing (figurative) Gen 1:14 ; Lev 10:10 , and of judging, knowing, teaching, etc., if the idea of distinguishing be involved, as Gen 16:5 ; 2Sam 19:36 לְרָע טוֺב בֵּין הַאֵדַע can I discern between good and evil ? 1Kin 3:9 ; Jonah 4:11 ; Gen 31:49 (watch between ), Judg 11:10 (hear), Josh 22:27 (witness), Isa 2:4 and he shall judge (arbitrate) between the nations, 5:3 ; Lev 27:33 ; Ezek 44:23 ; Mal 3:18 ; 2Chr 14:10 (see RV); and in other metaphoric applications, as of a covenant or sign between two contracting parties, Gen 9:12 , 15 ; Exod 31:13 +; or an oath Gen 26:28 ; 2Sam 21:7 ; enmity or strife Gen 3:15 ; 13:7 ; Deut 25:1 ; Prov 6:19 ; peace 1 Kings 5:26; good-will 14:9 . &#8212; It is used of time in the phrase of P הָעַרְבַּיִם בֵּין (see below עֶרֶב ), & Neh 5:18 יָמִים עֲשֶׂרֶת בֵּין during the interval of ten days, i.e. every ten days (unusual).With other prepositions: — a. אֶלבֵּֿין , after a verb implying motion, in between, in among Ezek 31:10 , 14 . So לְ אֶלבֵּֿינוֺת ib. 10:2 . b. בְּבֵן Isa 44:4 in the midst of, amongst ( ᵐ5 Ew Di Che חָצִיר מַיִם כְּבֵין ). c. עַלבֵּֿין nearly as אֶלבֵּֿין Ezek 19:11 d. מִבֵּין from between: Gen 49:10 nor the ruler's staff רַגְלָיו מִבֵּין from between his feet (where, as the king sits in state, he holds it), Exod 25:22 from between the cherubim (so Num 7:89 ), Hosea 2:4 ; Zech 6:1 ; 9:7 ; Deut 28:57 the after-birth רַגְלֶיהָ מִבֵּין הַיּוֺצֵת that cometh forth from between her feet, i.e. from her womb (compare Il. 19. 10 πεσεῖν μετὰ ποσσὶ γυναικός ) Repeated 2Kin 16:14 to specify the two objects from between which a thing is moved. Ezek 47:18 is difficult and uncertain: see Commentaries Less precisely from, the midst of: Num 17:2 הַשְּׂרֵפָה מִבֵּין out of the midst of the burning, Psa 104:12 עֳפָאִים מִבֵּין from amongst the branches they utter their song, Jer 48:45 and a flame סִיחוֺן מִבֵּין from the midst of Sihon (Sihon representing his people: but expression is singular; read perhaps ס ׳מִבֵּית , compare Num 21:28 ס ׳מִקִּרְיַת : || in both passages מֵחֶשְׁבּוֺן ), Ezek 37:21 . e. לְ מִבֵּינוֺת from between Ezek 10:2 , 6 (twice in verse); 10:7 . 2 Dual בֵּנַ֫יִם space between two armies (= Greek μεταίχμιον ), 1Sam 17:4 , 23 הַבֵּנַיִם אִישׁ man of the μεταίχμιον , i.e. champion (of Goliath). בֵּית feminine of בֵּין בַּיִן, (Nö M 194 f. ; Syriac often, PS 470 ) preposition between Ezek 41:9 b (to be joined with 41:10 ; see RVm), unless indeed a mere error for בֵּין (which Ezekiel often uses); also Prov 8:2 accusative To ᵐ5 ( ἀνὰ μέσον ) ᵑ9 ᵑ7 Hi Ew §217 g ; and Job 8:17 according to ᵐ5 Ew Di 1 (Di 2undecided ). בֵּין preposition between (Biblical Hebrew [ בַּ֫יִן ,] בֵּין ; בֵּינֵי בֵּין, ᵑ7, Syriac , ), Dan 7:5 ; with suffix 3plural masculine בֵּינֵיהוֺן 7:7 Kt (Qr 3 plural feminine בֵּינֵיהֵן ).","rootNote":"(sometimes in the plural masculine or feminine); properly, the constructive form of an otherwise unused noun from 995 ; a distinction; but used only as a preposition,","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 21 16","keyReferences":["1Chr 21 16","1Chr 21 16","1Kgs 3 9","1Kgs 5 26","1Kgs 5 26","1Kgs 7 28","1Kgs 7 29","1Kgs 7 46"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":410,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 21 16","book":"1Chr","chapter":21,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בֵּ֤ין","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR"},{"reference":"1Chr 21 16","book":"1Chr","chapter":21,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/בֵ֣ין","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/R"},{"reference":"1Kgs 3 9","book":"1Kgs","chapter":3,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בֵּֽין","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR"},{"reference":"1Kgs 5 26","book":"1Kgs","chapter":5,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בֵּ֤ין","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR"},{"reference":"1Kgs 5 26","book":"1Kgs","chapter":5,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/בֵ֣ין","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/R"},{"reference":"1Kgs 7 28","book":"1Kgs","chapter":7,"verse":28,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בֵּ֥ין","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR"},{"reference":"1Kgs 7 29","book":"1Kgs","chapter":7,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בֵּ֣ין","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR"},{"reference":"1Kgs 7 46","book":"1Kgs","chapter":7,"verse":46,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בֵּ֥ין","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR"},{"reference":"1Kgs 7 46","book":"1Kgs","chapter":7,"verse":46,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/בֵ֥ין","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/R"},{"reference":"1Kgs 14 30","book":"1Kgs","chapter":14,"verse":30,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בֵין","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR"},{"reference":"1Kgs 14 30","book":"1Kgs","chapter":14,"verse":30,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/בֵ֥ין","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/R"},{"reference":"1Kgs 15 6",